# Trivy ignore file — documented, time-bounded suppressions.
# Each entry records WHY a finding is accepted and the trigger to revisit it.
# Reviewed every release; remove entries the moment the upstream gate clears.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# starlette 1.x advisories — UPSTREAM-GATED (cannot remediate yet).
#
# The fixed starlette releases (1.1.0 / 1.3.1) require fastapi >= 0.137, which
# introduced the internal `_IncludedRouter` route type. That type subclasses
# Starlette's BaseRoute but carries no `.path` attribute. prometheus-fastapi-
# instrumentator (through its latest, 8.0.0) resolves every request's route
# name by iterating `app.routes` and reading `route.path`, so it raises
# AttributeError on every request once `_IncludedRouter` is present — breaking
# the /metrics middleware app-wide. FreeSDN is therefore held on fastapi 0.136.x
# / starlette 0.52.1 until the instrumentator handles the new route type.
# See backend/pyproject.toml for the matching version pins and rationale.
#
# Applicability of the two flagged HIGH advisories to FreeSDN's deployment:
#   CVE-2026-48818 — SSRF / NTLM credential theft via UNC paths in StaticFiles
#       on Windows. FreeSDN ships and runs as Linux containers; there are no
#       Windows UNC paths in the deployment surface. Not exploitable here.
#   CVE-2026-54283 — request.form() size limits ignored for
#       application/x-www-form-urlencoded (DoS). FreeSDN's API is JSON-first and
#       sits behind a reverse proxy that enforces request body-size limits.
#
# Revisit trigger: prometheus-fastapi-instrumentator ships `_IncludedRouter`
# support (or we migrate metrics off it) -> bump fastapi/starlette and delete
# these two lines.
CVE-2026-48818
CVE-2026-54283

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# caddy edge binary — Go stdlib advisory, UPSTREAM-GATED (cannot remediate yet).
#
# CVE-2026-42504 — net/textproto MIME header decode (DoS) in the Go stdlib that
# the official caddy:2.11.4-alpine image is compiled with (Go 1.26.3; fixed in
# Go 1.26.4). 2.11.4 is the latest caddy release, so the bundled toolchain only
# advances when caddy publishes a rebuild. The edge image already runs
# `apk upgrade` for OS packages (openssl, etc.); the caddy binary itself is the
# remaining gap. Exposure is limited: the edge terminates TLS and reverse-proxies
# trusted internal services; it is not a general-purpose mail/MIME processor.
#
# Revisit trigger: caddy ships a release built with Go >= 1.26.4 -> bump the
# `caddy:` base tag in frontend/Dockerfile and delete this line.
CVE-2026-42504
